{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>You will surely wear away.</b> As the Targum renders it — and its meaning is a term of wearing away, פלייש\"טרא בְּלַעַז, as in ״וְהֶעָלֶה נָבֵל״ (Jeremiah 8), ״כִּנְבֹל עָלֶה מִגֶּפֶן״ (Isaiah 34) — which dries out from the heat and from the cold, and its strength fails and it grows weary." "<b>Also you.</b> To include Aaron and Hur and the seventy elders." "<b>Too heavy for you.</b> Its weight is greater than your strength."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French *fleistrir*, 'to wilt/wither'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:00.959318735Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}